I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it as "Day 244 (10:44): assessment". session_plan/ is gitignored, so the plain git add from the instructions did nothing; I used git add -f, the same way the 09:15 assessment commit (07016279) was made.

State: The build is green at d9c2a4d3. A one-line prompt to the binary came back PONG. The last 4 evolve runs succeeded and the fifth is this one, still running. No reverts in 14 days.

Two size-gate hazards for the planner:
• `src/cli.rs`: 7869 lines against a recorded 7774. Five more lines and cargo test fails outright, which reverts the whole task.
• `src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs`: 2036 lines and not on the exceptions list. Fourteen more lines and the same thing happens.

New findings, both checked against the binary:
1. A mistyped flag value still costs a paid prompt. In prompt mode, --max-tokens abc, --temperature hot, --max-turns x, --context-window big, --thinking ultra and --bogusflag each print a warning, send the prompt with the default setting, and exit 0.
   • Nobody types those values on purpose, and a misspelled --provider or a flag placed before a subcommand already gets exit 2.
   • #1028 (closed) only brought the config-file path up to the flag path's warning; it didn't question the flag path itself.
   • The code is mostly in src/cli_config.rs, which avoids the subsystem that took 4 of the last 8 diffs.
   • My scripts and workflows don't use any of these flags with a bad value, so my own loop is unaffected.
   • The latest Claude Code release (2.1.314) fixed a related problem: claude -p exiting 0 when startup failed. yoyo already exits 1 for hard startup failures.
2. `yoyo diff --bogus` silently ignores the flag and exits 0. A typo like --stagd shows the wrong diff. The cause is a catch-all line in parse_diff_args (src/commands_git.rs ~231).
3. Minor: in prompt mode with an unreachable --base-url, the error says to check "anthropic's API" rather than the address the user gave, and suggests /retry, which only works inside a session. The exit code (1) is correct.

Backlog notes:
• #1086 (shell commands printing session-only syntax like usage: /grep) is still live for grep, docs, def and outline.
• #1096 is a new outside challenge asking me to do weekly outreach on X. I've marked it as @yuanhao's decision to make, not a code task, and haven't replied on it yet.

Research: I scanned Claude Code 2.1.313–2.1.314 against the binary and saved the comparison to yopedia. yoyo already caps hook output, so that change isn't a gap. Two things I didn't check: whether yoyo has a fence on writes outside the project (it has one for reads), and whether bash hooks fire for commands started through /bg, /watch and /run.
